										"Events": [],
										"Text":
										{
											"$text": "# VLF TERMINAL SYSTEM – README\r\n\r\nWelcome to the VLF Secure Operations Terminal.\r\n\r\nThis terminal operates under the authority of the Vietnamese Liberation Front and is reserved for trusted personnel only. Unauthorized access is a breach of operational protocol. All usage is monitored and archived by the Internal Oversight Division.\r\n\r\n## SYSTEM FUNCTIONS\r\n\r\n- **read** – View the contents of a file  \r\n- **run** – Execute scripts or VLF-compatible operations  \r\n- **scan** – Analyze files for intel, threats, or encoded data  \r\n- **download** – Save files from the terminal to your local cache  \r\n\r\nNeed assistance? Use the `help` command for more detailed instructions.\r\n\r\n## USER LEVELS\r\n\r\n- Guest: Limited access to general notices and surface-level records  \r\n- Admin: Full system authority, including access to encrypted data and override commands\r\n\r\n## CODE OF CONDUCT\r\n\r\n- Confirm your clearance before issuing commands  \r\n- Never share credentials or transfer them via unsecured channels  \r\n- Report suspicious terminal behavior to Command Liaison using form CL-09  \r\n- If you suspect infiltration or compromise, initiate Contingency Protocol Blackline immediately\r\n\r\n## SUPPORT CONTACT\r\n\r\nFor technical issues, submit a secured query through Node V-42 or contact Engineering Command directly.\r\n\r\n## FINAL NOTICE\r\n\r\nThis terminal is an asset of the Vietnamese Liberation Front. Tampering, unauthorized use, or compromise will be treated as an internal threat and handled accordingly.\r\n\r\nVLF — The Red River is ours.\r\n\r\n> END OF FILE",
											"$ns": "[680EB13DB6AABA9D965D692ABD17282F]",
											"$key": "BDC95BBC428DC3D8EEE56AB02EDD2BCA"
										}
									}
								]
							}
